          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Which chapter holds high blood pressure, and what does that chapter deliberately exclude?",
          "answer": "Hypertension (high blood pressure) is coded in the circulatory system chapter, ICD-10-CM Chapter 9 (I00-I99). The hypertension coding summary places the basic code, I10, there, and the family of related codes I11 to I16 covers hypertension that affects the heart or kidneys, or that has a known underlying cause. (Source: *Coding hypertension: I10 and the hypertensive disease family*; *ICD-10-CM Chapter 9: diseases of the circulatory system*.)\n\nThe retrieved passages do not say what Chapter 9 deliberately excludes. The excerpt I received begins partway through its introduction, and the exclusion notes were not included, so I can't answer that part from these results. The passages do show one related boundary. An elevated blood-pressure reading in someone who has no hypertension diagnosis is classed among symptoms and abnormal findings in ICD-10-CM Chapter 18 (R00-R99), not in the circulatory chapter. (Source: *ICD-10-CM Chapter 18: symptoms, signs and abnormal findings*.)\n\nFor the full list of exclusions, the official ICD-10-CM tabular list for Chapter 9 would need to be checked, ideally with a coder or clinician.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
